<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36399" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνυπάρχω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>exist</i> or <i>be present in,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἔμβρυον τὸ ἐνυπάρχον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>HA</u>
					577a14
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-άρχουσα ψυχή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Epicur.
					<u>Ep.</u>
					1p.21U.
				</span></i>
			
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>to be immanent</i> or <i>inherent,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ πρῶτον ἐ.,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕλη</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				193a10
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				194b24
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν ἅπαντι χρόνῳ τὸ [νῦν]
			ἐ.</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				233b35
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξ ὧν</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στοιχείων</span>)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> ἔστι
				τὰ ὄντα ἐνυπαρχόντων</span>
			<i>the inherence</i> whereof is the cause of existences, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Metaph.</u>
				998a31
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				1014a26
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plot.
				5.3.11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Jul.
				<u>Or.</u>
				4.140c
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> in
			Logic, <i>to be contained in, inhere,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνυπάρχειν τοῖς κατηγορουμένοις ἢ
				ἐνυπάρχεσθαι,</span> of the predicates, <i>to be contained
				in</i> the subjects or <i>to have</i> them <i>inhering,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>APo.</u>
				73b17
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ἐν τῷ τί ἐστι</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				84a25
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν τῷ λόγῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Metaph.</u>
					1022n29
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς ὅροις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>APr.</u>
					28a6
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
